    {
      "id": "02-open",
      "instruction": "In Odoo, open the Sales app and create a new quotation. Set the Customer field to '{{runid}} Bench Customer' — it is an autocomplete dropdown, so type the name and actually select the matching option from the dropdown so the value is properly set. In the Order Lines table, add ONE order line: pick any product from the product catalogue (choose it from the product dropdown, not just typed), and set its Quantity to 3. Let the app fill in the unit price automatically. Then report: (a) the exact product name you chose, (b) the unit price the app filled in for that line, and (c) the Untaxed Amount shown in the totals section. Do not confirm the quotation — leave it as a draft quotation. Do not wait for network idle (the app long-polls); wait for concrete page elements instead.",
      "skill": "s_7dc11c",
      "params": {
        "v1": "{{runid}} Bench Customer",
        "v2": "{{runid}}"
      },
